\subsection{Robustness under deployment stress: imbalance and federation}

Two stressors closer to deployment separate the representations more sharply than the
balanced benchmark. \rev{Under imbalance the cheap features overtake the foundation embedding;
under simulated federation the two means are close and the cheap features retain a larger
fraction of their centralized ARI and a higher worst-case partition.} First, class imbalance. At the
natural-like 9:1 SR:AF ratio (majority 0.90), every representation's ARI falls, because
isolating a 10\% minority cluster with a partitional method is intrinsically hard, but the
hand-crafted features retain the most structure \rev{over the ten seeds (ARI 0.265 [0.250,
0.280], AMI 0.245 [0.233, 0.257]) and now \emph{overtake} ECGFounder (ARI 0.063 [0.061, 0.065],
AMI 0.148 [0.143, 0.152]), with no overlap between the two ARI intervals. HuBERT-ECG reaches the
same ARI as ECGFounder (0.061 [0.053, 0.069]) at a lower AMI (0.044 [0.037, 0.050]), and the raw
and conv-AE pipelines stay at chance (0.000 and 0.004).} The foundation embedding's balanced-data
lead does not survive imbalance.

Second, federation. Under IID federation across ten sites, every representation retains
essentially its centralized ARI, which validates the federated procedure
(Table~\ref{tab:fed}; Fig.~\ref{fig:fed}). Non-IID client heterogeneity degrades all
representations, but unequally. The hand-crafted features are the most robust, retaining
92\% of their centralized ARI (0.644 to 0.591). ECGFounder's centralized advantage erodes
from 0.885 to 0.612. \rev{The two means are close, 0.612 against 0.591, and they do not carry
the same risk. Across the ten redrawn site partitions the hand-crafted bootstrap interval is
[0.546, 0.631] and the worst single partition still returns 0.455, whereas ECGFounder's interval
is [0.382, 0.796] and three of its ten partitions fall to 0.132 or below, one of them to chance. A
deployment claim rests on the worst site draw rather than on the average one, and on that
reading the 16 hand-crafted features are the more predictable of the two under site
heterogeneity.} Across both stressors the compact interpretable representation is the more
dependable choice for privacy-preserving, multi-site phenotyping.

\begin{table}[t]
\centering
\caption{Federated robustness: mean ARI over ten seeds and ten simulated sites.
Retention is the ratio of non-IID to centralized ARI.}
\label{tab:fed}
\begin{tabular}{lcccc}
\toprule
Representation & centralized & federated IID & federated non-IID & retention \\
\midrule
ECGFounder   & 0.885 & 0.885 & 0.612 & 0.69 \\
hand-crafted & 0.644 & 0.643 & 0.591 & \textbf{0.92} \\
HuBERT-ECG   & 0.174 & 0.172 & 0.106 & 0.61 \\
raw-flatten  & 0.000 & 0.000 & 0.000 & N/A \\
\bottomrule
\end{tabular}
\end{table}

