\subsection{Deployment cost}

\rev{The deployability claim is about cost as well as accuracy, so Table~\ref{tab:cost} states
what each representation costs to compute. The two are ordered against each other: ECGFounder,
which clusters best, is the most expensive per record, fifteen times the hand-crafted extraction,
and both foundation models need a gigabyte or more of resident
memory against \mbox{364\,MB} for the hand-crafted path, which carries no learned parameters at
all. Clustering itself is negligible everywhere, under \mbox{0.3\,s} for the whole cohort at any
of the five dimensionalities, so the cost of a representation is the cost of extracting it.}

